      "id": 496184,
      "username": "sine387",
      "name": "Sine",
      "created_at": "2026-03-22T08:38:33.680Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Yeah this smells like ERPNext losing track of sub assembly links, not your stock. That error usually pops when the system didn’t actually fetch or sync the sub assembly items into the plan, even if they exist in BOM. Try hitting “Get Items from BOM” again or just recreate the plan clean, I’ve had cases where one stale reference breaks the whole reserve step. Also double check default warehouse on sub assemblies, if that’s empty or mismatched it silently fails and then throws this random message, super annoying lol.</p>",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/s/df788c/{size}.png",
